@@ -0,0 +1,13 @@
+# G PC Health 0.17.1 — missing-evidence candidate
+
+This isolated candidate is based on ca354d2194a454b0356057c2db34e94cea8ffbbe. It retains the corrected named tabs, fixed footer and Huawei BCD correction. It is not a source publication or production release.
+
+Unknown security controls now expose an additive explanation: a stable reason code, retained source identities or an explicit “not recorded”, and localized manual next steps. Only explicit collector state/error tokens establish denial, timeout, cancellation, missing observation, unsupported fields or conflict. Missing administrator policy differs from unreadable/wrong-type policy. Empty or generic evidence remains “cause not established”; Unknown never means protection or a BIOS password is absent. Scores, weights, statuses, coverage and original observations are unchanged. Complete selectable row details, HTML, JSON and clipboard retain the explanation and raw evidence.
+
+Triage distinguishes incomplete collection/coverage from a checked assessment without significant findings. Missing technical signals receive the same honest source limits and safe guidance; the application does not invent a failed provider or an access requirement. CRIT/WARN ordering and health/security separation remain unchanged.
+
+A compact Overview symptom menu opens existing performance, incident, resource-probe and printing diagnostics. Selecting a route records the original symptom note for JSON/HTML/clipboard, does not alter an action batch or run repairs, and leaves the destination idle until an explicit user operation. Existing Common Problems menu behavior is retained; only the symptom route requests its idle mode. The footer remains outside scrolling.
+
+Actual portable source-linked checks: behavior RED 1/10 → GREEN 10/10; unchanged security evaluator 9/9. Existing guidance/triage harness has seven failures on Linux, reproduced identically against the exact parent (12/19 guidance cases); these are not represented as passing or changed to green. Complete Windows-target cross-build uses SDK 8.0.425 and warnings as errors. Exact commands, logs, final publication identity, source bundle and binary checksum are retained in the external immutable handoff, avoiding a circular self-SHA.
+
+Windows runtime, all WinForms/selftests/rendered screenshots, ancestor clipping, busy progress, native DPI/RDP, UAC, Huawei device checks and Windows 11 pilot are NOT_RUN. Independent SPEC/QUALITY and owner integration remain pending. The original CI6 Git receive-pack outcome remains UNKNOWN; this local artifact does not reconcile it or authorize a retry. CDC 2.12.1 and shared source remain unchanged.
